  "live_records": {
    "q-95901": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95901",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the singular value decomposition $A=UΣ{V}^{T},$ where $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $Σ$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix\n- $U$ is a diagonal matrix",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $m\\times n$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $m\\times m$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $n\\times n$ matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $Σ$ must be a $3\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix,the matrix $V$ in the singular value decomposition $UΣ{V}^{T}$ must be orthogonal $4\\times 4$ matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $U$ must be orthogonal but not necessarily diagonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
