    "q-95902": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95902",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}\\,∗\\, & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\,∗\\, & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $V$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ which of the following could be the first column of the matrix $V?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that since $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ the matrix $V$ must be a $2\\times 2$ orthogonal matrix. This means that \n\n- the first column must be orthogonal to the second column, and\n\n- the norm of the first column must be equal to $1.$\n\nAmong the given options, only the vector $[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$ has both properties.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
